Read a subagent's model and identity only from the tool call that actually
launched it. Every tool_use block was kept as a possible launch and then read as
if it were the delegation tool's input, so a nested context spawned by any other
tool picked up whatever argument happened to be named `model` and wrote it to
`gen_ai.request.model` — always emitted, and a metric dimension, so arbitrary tool
arguments landed in metric cardinality. Only `Agent` and `Task`, the two names the
CLI itself resolves a `subagent_type` for, are read that way now.

`gen_ai.agent.name` on an `execute_tool` span is also the agent that ran the tool,
so a tool invoked by a `code-reviewer` subagent is attributed to it rather than to
the run's own agent.
